WEBVTT

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:02.350
Well, let's get crackin'.

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:03.950
Let's-a-go.

00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:05.920
Stop messing around and start!

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:08.990
The ambiguous 3cm?
Does that mean it's plushy? Wait!

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:12.330
The wrapping is a uniform, argh,
it's not an act, pooh

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:13.890
Gotta do your best, gotta just do it

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:15.530
That's time to catch 'n' release, eek

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:17.190
Between sweat (whoop)
sweat (whoop)

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:20.600
Darlin', darlin', freeze!

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:26.580
Kinda lethargic,
something's kinda comin' out

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:28.550
I love you... Oh wait,
one of those was different

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:29.780
Worrywarts, high metal bars

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:31.580
Tasty thoughts... And that's enough!

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:33.390
The heated body of that
flying you-know-who

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:34.920
It's what you call a normal girlie

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.130
Am I the only one surprised?

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:37.390
Seconds on pork-bone broth ramen
with wire-hard noodles

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:38.320
Da da da da da

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.360
Pom-poms cheer squad

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:47.930
Let's get cherry pie

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:49.570
Happy fun welcoming party

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:51.140
Look up! Sensation

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:54.140
Yeah! Feeling of existence,
dot dot small planet

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:55.740
Collided and it melted away,
in total awe

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:57.510
Go all out to sing, shi-ranger!

00:00:57.510 --> 00:00:58.680
Take it away!

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:03.150
I should be the one who'll be laughing in the end

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:10.360
Because I have the sailor suit
<- This is my conclusion

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:12.360
It's only Monday!

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:15.910
Already in a bad mood? What to do?

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:22.870
I really prefer the summer outfits
<- kya! wah! good! (cute!)

00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:25.920
Until we approach 3 pixels,
no hesitations please *

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:27.540
Do your best, be energetic

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:29.730
My darlin', darlin' please!

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:33.490
On your mark!

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:34.880
Get set!

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:45.730
You've done it again, Kona-chan.

00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:47.100
That was amazing.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.400
How come you aren't on any sports teams...

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:52.010
...when you're so athletic?

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:54.270
'Cause if I join a team...

00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:57.530
...I'll miss my prime time anime.

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:08.460
Say, Tsukasa.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:10.800
Which end of a chocolate cornet do you start from?

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:13.540
The head, I suppose.

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:15.050
I see.

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:17.060
By the way...

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:18.270
Which side's the head?

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:19.930
The fat end or the thin end?

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:24.570
I would guess the thin end.

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:25.690
Oh.

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:28.600
I thought it was the fat end.

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:31.380
But why would the thin end be the head?

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:33.490
Well, doesn't it look like a seashell?

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:35.900
Why did you think it was the fat end, Kona-chan?

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:36.890
'Cause, you know...

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:38.570
It looks like a caterpillar?

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:39.880
A caterpillar?

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:43.570
But I guess it works better if you picture a seashell.

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:00.420
U-Um...

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:03.090
You could cut off the thin end...

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:06.290
...and eat it with the excess chocolate.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:08.730
Now I get it.

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:13.730
Good thinking, Miyuki-san.

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:14.910
You're so smart.

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:15.620
Not at all.

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:18.150
Everyone has their own approach to eating.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.360
How do you eat cream puffs?

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:22.740
Cream puffs, you ask?

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:23.890
Well...

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:26.370
I start by splitting it in half...

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:29.460
...and eating the lid after dipping it
in the cream from the bottom...

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:33.250
And then I eat the bottom half.

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:36.540
This way, I don't have to worry
about any cream spilling out...

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:39.840
...while maintaining a balance between cream and puff.

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:45.160
What about the ones that have
both custard and cream inside?

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:46.940
How do you eat those?

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:47.980
Do you mix them up?

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:48.610
No.

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:50.690
I wouldn't do such a thing.

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:53.740
But how would you mix them?

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:54.980
Just asking.

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:57.310
When do you eat the strawberry on a strawberry shortcake...

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:59.480
...or the chestnut on top of a Mont Blanc?

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:01.020
Let's see...

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:05.700
There are also strawberries tucked
between layers of sponge cake.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:11.240
I follow a normal distribution of
strawberry, cream, and cake as I eat.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:16.080
So there isn't a set time for eating the strawberry.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:17.980
You really know your stuff.

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:21.840
I always save the strawberry for last.

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:24.350
But then I get full sometimes...

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:25.670
...so I end up not eating it...

00:04:25.670 --> 00:04:27.810
...or someone in my family takes it.

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:30.990
Your favorites hafta come first.

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:35.020
Actually, I don't think I've ever seen
anyone take a strawberry from Sis.

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:36.060
That's Kagami for you.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:37.170
Doesn't miss a step.

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:41.550
Are you able to eat the last bite of a popsicle without dropping it?

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:42.900
Dropping it?

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:44.780
If you aren't careful...

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:48.030
...you drop the last bit, right?

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:50.380
What do you do, Kona-chan?

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:52.080
Suck it down to nothing.

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:55.900
You could rotate the popsicle as you eat.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:57.440
That's a good idea.

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:01.040
I'm not very fond of ice cream cones.

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:01.750
Why?

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:05.800
I can't stand it when only the cone is left.

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:06.980
That's right.

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:09.380
You always end up with some cone left.

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:14.060
I push the ice cream into the cone as I eat.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:16.810
How do you push the ice cream?

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:19.060
I do a little push and pull action as I eat.

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:21.280
Push and pull, is it?

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:23.940
Yuki-chan prioritizes balance, right?

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:24.770
That's right.

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:27.160
Then what do you do with curry rice?

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:28.990
Do you mix the sauce with the rice?

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:29.970
No.

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:31.710
I dont mix them...

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:33.530
...but I make sure that they're equally proportioned.

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:35.390
I mix mine up.

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:36.290
What about you, Kona-chan?

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:37.820
Depends on the curry.

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:40.200
If there's any Worcester sauce or raw egg in it...

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:41.790
...I guess I do a little mixy-wixy.

00:05:41.790 --> 00:05:43.070
Worcester sauce in curry?

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:44.670
It's good stuff.

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:46.960
Do you also put Worcester sauce on your fried eggs?

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:49.340
I put soy sauce on fried eggs.

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:51.800
I use mayonnaise.

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:53.410
On your fried eggs?

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:54.800
I don't mean boiled eggs.

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:56.850
You see, mayonnaise...

00:05:56.850 --> 00:05:58.520
...goes well with most egg dishes.

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:00.020
Do you put it on your curry?

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:03.500
It's a must on white rice.

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:06.500
But the sweetness also goes well with beef bowls.

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:07.780
It's also good with parent-child bowls.

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:10.610
You know how eggs and
chicken meat are child and parent.

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:13.980
So once I add mayonnaise, which is made from eggs...

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:14.020
...I call it an expanded family bowl.
So once I add mayonnaise, which is made from eggs...

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:17.120
...I call it an expanded family bowl.

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:18.990
Also...

00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:20.520
I usually can't stand natto...

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:22.610
...but I was able to eat it once I added mayonnaise.

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:24.690
Can't imagine it.

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:25.520
But...

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:29.690
...putting mayonnaise on soft-boiled eggs might be best.

00:06:29.690 --> 00:06:32.170
The fried eggs at my house are also half-done.

00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:35.200
It's how my dad likes them.

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:38.750
He likes to suck out the yolk.

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:42.310
And if it's overcooked, he can't suck the yolk.

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:44.520
What about skewered chicken?

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:45.710
What about it?

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:47.450
Do you leave it on the spit?

00:06:47.450 --> 00:06:49.320
Or do you use chopsticks to take it off?

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:51.000
Let's see...

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:54.110
If I'm eating one by myself, I leave it on the spit.

00:06:54.110 --> 00:06:56.660
But if I'm with other people, I'll take it off.

00:06:56.660 --> 00:06:57.810
Yeah, yeah.

00:06:57.810 --> 00:07:00.160
Isn't it a little awkward when there's only one left?

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:03.710
I can't bring myself to take the last one.

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:06.580
As time goes by without anyone eating it...

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:09.330
It starts getting dry...

00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:10.960
...and looking anything but appetizing...

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:12.740
...and no one's willing to make a move...

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:13.810
...but when the busboy takes it, yo go...

00:07:13.810 --> 00:07:15.700
"Wait, we're not done with that yet."

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:17.180
...kinda on reflex.

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:20.360
But then you end up leaving without eating it.

00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:21.920
Such a waste.

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:24.130
I feel sorry for it.

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:26.090
And when you grill meat...

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:29.690
...I feel sorry for the meat that's
all charred and stuck to the grill.

00:07:29.690 --> 00:07:33.230
You have to eat while you're grilling and chatting...

00:07:33.230 --> 00:07:34.900
...so it's a busy ordeal.

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:38.660
It's even worse with onion beef
tongue slices since they're done in'no time.

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:40.160
You're right.

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:40.170
They're done after just one flip.
You're right.

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:43.160
They're done after just one flip.

00:07:43.630 --> 00:07:44.870
Flip?

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:46.670
Onion beef tongue slices?

00:07:47.170 --> 00:07:49.670
You can't flip those.

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:51.130
Really?

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:52.620
If you flip them over...

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:55.140
...the onions on top will fall off.

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:56.620
Oh, yeah.

00:07:56.620 --> 00:08:01.310
They'll finish cooking without any flipping.

00:08:01.310 --> 00:08:02.460
I see...

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:04.090
I'll do that from now on.

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:06.450
You can never flip them.

00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:08.030
Really...

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:16.580
By the way, is the fat end or thin
end the head of a chocolate cornet?

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:19.370
Super bad boy.

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:22.640
There've been a bunch of kidnapping cases recently.

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:26.580
Guys forcing girls to address
them as "Master" and stuff.

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:28.370
Isn't that less...

00:08:28.370 --> 00:08:29.440
...an issue of morals...

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:32.420
...and more an issue of playing too
many dating sims and adult games?

00:08:32.420 --> 00:08:34.050
It's a commonly used scenario.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:36.820
Aren't you talking about yourself?!

00:08:38.270 --> 00:08:39.300
Er, wait a tick.

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:41.360
Why are you so well-versed in the adult game scenarios...

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:42.480
...Miss High School Second-year?

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:51.450
Your grades are always so good.

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:54.910
Don't you have any faults, Miyuki-san?

00:08:54.910 --> 00:08:56.580
I'm ashamed to say...

00:08:56.580 --> 00:08:59.090
...that I have a tendency to brood over things...

00:08:59.090 --> 00:09:01.120
...or space out.

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:03.850
I've cut my finger while using a slicer.

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:04.440
Ow!

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:08.120
And tripped over myself while in a hurry.

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:11.780
And gotten my bag stuck in the door on a train.

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:13.500
Miyuki-san.

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:17.380
Those aren't faults, but elements of turning people on.

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:18.430
Turn-ons?

00:09:18.430 --> 00:09:19.630
The clumsy factor.

00:09:19.630 --> 00:09:22.890
<i>What was going on inside
Kona-chan's head during all that?!</i>

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:26.250
Miyuki-san, why do you wear
glasses when you're actually attractive?

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:28.500
You'll only nab a niche audience.

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:29.640
Nab's a little...

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:32.450
Setting aside the issue of popularity...

00:09:32.450 --> 00:09:34.160
...why don't you wear contacts?

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:36.840
I heard that glasses make your vision worse.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:37.790
Um...

00:09:37.790 --> 00:09:40.490
I'm ashamed to be saying this in high school...

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:42.380
B-But...

00:09:42.380 --> 00:09:43.740
I'm...

00:09:43.740 --> 00:09:44.960
Scared!

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:46.420
Of contacts!

00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:47.650
Or to be specific...

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:50.060
...putting things in my eyes.

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:52.790
I can never open my eyes when I'm underwater.

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:53.460
<i>Curses!</i>

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:55.230
<i>She's cute to the core!</i>

00:09:55.230 --> 00:09:56.260
<i>Must be innate.</i>

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:59.020
Isn't that Miyuki-san?

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:01.800
Is she here for an eye examination?

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:03.060
To get contacts?

00:10:05.770 --> 00:10:08.960
Miyuki-san's probably better off this way forever.

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:10.100
That looked painful...

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:11.690
A pillar of evolution.

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:16.200
Kagami's at home with a cold?

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:20.010
It looks like she doesn't have the flu though.

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:23.930
I'm stupid so I don't have
to worry about getting the flu.

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:26.130
I've heard that applies to colds...

00:10:26.130 --> 00:10:28.400
...but it also applies to the flu?

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:32.890
There's a difference between a cold and the flu?

00:10:32.890 --> 00:10:35.030
I thought the flu was like a super cold.

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:37.700
I-I think they're different...

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:41.090
But now I'm not sure anymore...

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:44.130
The difference between the flu and a cold?

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:46.850
Well...

00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:49.640
The flu is caused by a virus.

00:10:49.640 --> 00:10:52.770
The symptoms are a fever
and aching throughout the body.

00:10:52.770 --> 00:10:55.740
And there is a risk of complications.

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:56.500
On the other hand...

00:10:56.500 --> 00:10:59.120
...the symptoms of a cold are
a sore throat and runny nose...

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:01.230
...and the fever doesn't run as high.

00:11:01.230 --> 00:11:03.860
And there are a number of other minute differences.

00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:06.230
Which is why...

00:11:06.230 --> 00:11:08.600
...they are different illnesses.

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:10.240
I see...

00:11:11.390 --> 00:11:12.410
H-However...

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:15.270
Well, they share many similarities...

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:19.100
...so you could possibly say that
it's an upgraded version of a cold...

00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:20.000
I see!

00:11:22.340 --> 00:11:22.860
Kona-chan.

00:11:22.860 --> 00:11:25.130
Whats with the pensive face?

00:11:25.130 --> 00:11:27.040
Oh, nothing big.

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:29.600
I was just curious about something
after our conversation this morning.

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:31.310
About a cold and the flu?

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:35.200
You didn't disagree when I said I was dumb.

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:36.060
N-No!

00:11:36.060 --> 00:11:37.230
It's not like that!

00:11:42.820 --> 00:11:43.900
Konata-chan.

00:11:43.900 --> 00:11:44.860
Welcome.

00:11:44.860 --> 00:11:46.910
She's here to visit Sis.

00:11:47.780 --> 00:11:49.200
Thank you for visiting.

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:49.830
It's nothing.

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:51.540
Sorry to intrude.

00:11:56.330 --> 00:11:58.750
Kagami actually looks pretty cute when she's asleep.

00:11:58.920 --> 00:11:59.630
What is it?!

00:11:59.630 --> 00:12:00.250
Why are you here?!

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:00.670
She's up. She's up.

00:12:00.670 --> 00:12:01.630
Get out!

00:12:02.340 --> 00:12:03.090
Visiting?

00:12:03.090 --> 00:12:03.920
You?

00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:05.340
For my sake?

00:12:05.670 --> 00:12:06.590
That's right.

00:12:06.590 --> 00:12:08.760
B-But I don't want you to catch the flu from me.

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:10.350
I appreciate the thought though.

00:12:10.890 --> 00:12:11.470
<i>Hah.</i>

00:12:11.470 --> 00:12:13.270
<i>You know you're happy about it.</i>

00:12:13.270 --> 00:12:15.430
<i>Is she worried about me...</i>

00:12:15.430 --> 00:12:17.650
<i>...because of the new virus going around?</i>

00:12:17.650 --> 00:12:21.570
<i>I figured she only ever had games and anime on her mind.</i>

00:12:21.570 --> 00:12:23.610
<i>I'm a little touched.</i>

00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:25.490
Well...

00:12:25.490 --> 00:12:28.410
I wanted to see your homework from the other day.

00:12:28.410 --> 00:12:30.280
And I got to see your face while you were sleeping...

00:12:30.320 --> 00:12:31.700
...so don't sweat it.

00:12:31.700 --> 00:12:32.240
Get out!

00:12:33.950 --> 00:12:34.950
Kagami!

00:12:34.950 --> 00:12:37.710
Miyuki-chan's here to visit you!

00:12:38.120 --> 00:12:38.960
Okay!

00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:40.420
I'm sorry to intrude.

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:43.000
Sorry you had to come on a day off.

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:45.260
Is it all right for you to be up?

00:12:45.260 --> 00:12:45.600
This is a little something.

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:46.470
Thanks.

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:48.430
I'm a lot better now.

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:50.300
My fever went down after I took some medicine.

00:12:50.300 --> 00:12:50.640
Here.

00:12:51.350 --> 00:12:53.180
Flowers and fruits! I'm overjoyed!

00:12:53.850 --> 00:12:54.850
Have a seat.

00:12:54.850 --> 00:12:56.540
Thank you very much.

00:12:56.540 --> 00:13:00.440
I intended to visit earlier
with Izumi-san and everyone...

00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:03.110
...but my schedule hasn't been very forgiving.

00:13:03.110 --> 00:13:04.230
S'okay. S'okay.

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:08.240
I brought some materials from the student council meeting.

00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:09.570
Thanks!

00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:13.950
If you could take a quick
glance without straining yourself...

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:18.080
Also, here are the budgets for each club.

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:20.750
And what else was there...

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:21.750
Um...

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:24.250
If I'm tiring you out...

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:25.880
...I'll leave.

00:13:26.090 --> 00:13:28.170
This is how a visit's supposed to be!

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:30.260
D-Did something happen?

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:32.970
Actually, Konata showed up yesterday...

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:36.140
It was like, good grief.

00:13:36.140 --> 00:13:40.020
That may just be how Izumi-san expresses herself.

00:13:40.600 --> 00:13:42.860
The homework may have been an attempt at humor...

00:13:42.860 --> 00:13:46.150
...in order to cheer you up.

00:13:46.150 --> 00:13:49.900
And perhaps she saw how your
face looked while you were sleeping...

00:13:49.900 --> 00:13:51.780
...because she didn't want to wake you up.

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:54.030
<i>Is this woman a saint?!</i>

00:13:54.030 --> 00:13:55.740
<i>That would've never occurred to me.</i>

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:57.160
Come to think of it...

00:13:57.160 --> 00:13:59.750
Is Tsukasa-san not here today?

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:02.020
Good morning.

00:14:02.370 --> 00:14:05.960
Are you feeling better, Sis?

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:10.050
As you can see...

00:14:10.050 --> 00:14:13.090
She's more laid-back than the person who's sick.

00:14:13.640 --> 00:14:14.930
U-Um...

00:14:14.930 --> 00:14:16.970
I'm not like this every morning...

00:14:16.970 --> 00:14:20.020
Just that I haven't really adjusted to daylight savings...

00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:21.940
It's a little late but welcome.

00:14:22.600 --> 00:14:23.940
I completely understand.

00:14:23.940 --> 00:14:26.570
I've been having a hard time waking up as well.

00:14:26.570 --> 00:14:28.190
Th-That's right.

00:14:28.190 --> 00:14:29.780
You get so sleepy these days.

00:14:29.780 --> 00:14:31.240
Indeed.

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:33.410
And it's especially warm today.

00:14:34.110 --> 00:14:34.990
That's the truth!

00:14:34.990 --> 00:14:36.280
It can't be helped.

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:39.200
And you know how our last day off was also warm?

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:42.920
When I woke up, it was already evening.

00:14:42.920 --> 00:14:45.130
I spent most of the time sleeping.

00:14:45.130 --> 00:14:47.920
It's good to rest when you have a day off.

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:51.010
So I ended up wearing my pajamas the whole day.

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:52.380
I guess I still am.

00:14:53.680 --> 00:14:56.420
Those are pajamas?

00:14:56.420 --> 00:14:57.760
That's right.

00:14:57.760 --> 00:14:59.470
They're quite adorable.

00:14:59.470 --> 00:15:01.100
I can't tell that they're pajamas.

00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:01.930
Really?

00:15:02.770 --> 00:15:04.650
I wonder if I can just stay in them.

00:15:05.100 --> 00:15:06.980
You could walk outside in them.

00:15:07.150 --> 00:15:08.150
Could I go into a convenience store in these?

00:15:08.150 --> 00:15:09.110
<i>It's like an endless loop of dumb and dumber!</i>

00:15:09.110 --> 00:15:10.690
Nobody would blink an eye.

00:15:12.530 --> 00:15:14.200
<i>It's gone up a little...</i>

00:15:15.320 --> 00:15:15.950
<i>No.</i>

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:17.030
<i>That might not be the case.</i>

00:15:17.030 --> 00:15:19.990
<i>I'm wearing a wired bra with extra padding...</i>

00:15:19.990 --> 00:15:21.620
<i>...which means extra weight.</i>

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:22.580
<i>That has to be it.</i>

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:24.670
<i>I wonder how many grams that adds.</i>

00:15:24.670 --> 00:15:26.170
<i>Once you subtract that...</i>

00:15:29.040 --> 00:15:30.460
<i>It's over...</i>

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:32.130
<i>I totally screwed up.</i>

00:15:32.130 --> 00:15:34.010
<i>I forgot we had examinations today...</i>

00:15:34.010 --> 00:15:36.680
<i>...so I wore my print underwear.</i>

00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:38.680
<i>I'm so embarrassed!</i>

00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:41.520
<i>I haven't grown at all...</i>

00:15:42.520 --> 00:15:43.350
Curses!

00:15:43.350 --> 00:15:45.850
You get to look all happy by yourself!

00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:47.060
Yo.

00:15:47.480 --> 00:15:48.320
I'm here.

00:15:48.320 --> 00:15:49.230
Sis.

00:15:49.610 --> 00:15:50.980
I was wondering.

00:15:51.730 --> 00:15:54.110
Kagami comes here a lot.

00:15:54.110 --> 00:15:56.160
Do you have no friends in your class?

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:57.780
Don't put me on your level.

00:15:57.780 --> 00:15:58.870
Are you trying to pick a fight?

00:15:59.000 --> 00:15:59.780
Oh.

00:15:59.780 --> 00:16:01.410
I thought you were being ostracized or something.

00:16:01.410 --> 00:16:02.490
Worry less about me...

00:16:02.490 --> 00:16:05.080
...and more about your lack of a social life.

00:16:05.340 --> 00:16:07.040
You don't have to worry about that.

00:16:07.420 --> 00:16:10.340
Believe it or not, I have around a hundred friends.

00:16:10.340 --> 00:16:13.590
And I'm pretty good at social dealings.

00:16:13.590 --> 00:16:15.590
And I'm in a party every night.

00:16:16.260 --> 00:16:18.780
My comrades and I strive
to recover the light stolen from

00:16:18.780 --> 00:16:21.050
the crystals to save the world from oblivion...

00:16:21.050 --> 00:16:22.100
...and rescue kidnapped princesses...

00:16:22.100 --> 00:16:23.640
Aren't you talking about a game?!

00:16:23.890 --> 00:16:26.230
I haven't seen that person in a while.

00:16:26.230 --> 00:16:26.850
Who?

00:16:26.890 --> 00:16:29.150
She's probably talking about some friend from a game.

00:16:30.110 --> 00:16:31.820
He plays a warrior.

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:37.810
He went somewhere with a lot of monsters to
train his battle skills, and I haven't seen him since.

00:16:39.300 --> 00:16:40.990
I heard from someone else...

00:16:40.990 --> 00:16:43.580
...that he was lying low in the sewers.

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:44.950
I wonder if he's okay.

00:16:44.950 --> 00:16:48.210
Everyone's worried since he hasn't come out.

00:16:48.210 --> 00:16:49.920
He isolated himself in the game?

00:16:50.130 --> 00:16:51.840
I don't know the details...

00:16:51.840 --> 00:16:55.800
...but his log-in info implies that he's been online the whole time.

00:16:55.800 --> 00:16:57.800
So he's isolated in both the real and virtual world?!

00:16:57.800 --> 00:17:00.140
Well, it's the same person in both cases.

00:17:00.430 --> 00:17:01.260
That's right...

00:17:01.260 --> 00:17:04.350
How did you two become friends?

00:17:04.810 --> 00:17:09.350
A huge fishy-looking foreigner
was about to take Tsukasa away...

00:17:09.350 --> 00:17:11.690
...when I happened to show up.

00:17:11.690 --> 00:17:13.190
Using my special fists of fury...

00:17:13.190 --> 00:17:15.320
...and beautiful hurricane kick...

00:17:15.320 --> 00:17:16.650
...I saved her.

00:17:16.650 --> 00:17:19.200
Why do we always end up talking about games?

00:17:19.400 --> 00:17:23.200
Well, that's what happens when
you run into an experienced fighter.

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:25.450
I'm not sure you should've
resorted to violence so quickly...

00:17:25.450 --> 00:17:26.620
...but you did a good thing.

00:17:26.910 --> 00:17:30.460
The foreigner was actually
just asking me for directions...

00:17:30.460 --> 00:17:33.500
...but I was having a hard time
understanding him when Kona-chan showed up...

00:17:33.500 --> 00:17:34.040
Hey!

00:17:34.040 --> 00:17:35.050
You were totally at fault there!

00:17:35.050 --> 00:17:36.630
And why do you look so proud about it?!

00:17:37.010 --> 00:17:40.340
It's that time of year again...

00:17:40.680 --> 00:17:42.010
Is something going to happen?

00:17:42.010 --> 00:17:42.640
No.

00:17:42.640 --> 00:17:44.810
I was thinking that the Tigers' season had started...

00:17:45.100 --> 00:17:48.520
You don't like watching sports, Kona-chan?

00:17:48.520 --> 00:17:50.350
You're really athletic...

00:17:50.350 --> 00:17:52.270
...so I thought you might enjoy it.

00:17:52.400 --> 00:17:55.110
Because if the game goes into extra innings...

00:17:55.110 --> 00:17:58.240
...the schedule for new anime gets all messed up.

00:17:58.570 --> 00:18:02.110
Sometimes, the show gets canceled altogether.

00:18:02.110 --> 00:18:05.160
It sucks when you lose something you like.

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:08.120
When do you eat the strawberry
on a strawberry shortcake, Kagami?

00:18:08.410 --> 00:18:09.120
Why you asking?

00:18:09.120 --> 00:18:12.460
I was wondering if you were the type to save your favorite for last.

00:18:12.460 --> 00:18:15.090
I usually eat my favorite stuff last...

00:18:15.090 --> 00:18:17.250
...but with strawberries, it depends on the situation.

00:18:17.250 --> 00:18:19.340
Then do you grill both sides of an onion beef tongue?

00:18:19.800 --> 00:18:21.130
Onion beef tongues?

00:18:22.130 --> 00:18:23.760
It's done in no time anyway...

00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:25.850
...but it'd go even faster if you did both sides.

00:18:25.850 --> 00:18:26.720
You can't.

00:18:26.720 --> 00:18:28.180
The onions will fall off.

00:18:28.180 --> 00:18:28.220
Don't you add the onions after the meat's done?
The onions will fall off.

00:18:28.220 --> 00:18:30.850
Don't you add the onions after the meat's done?

00:18:30.850 --> 00:18:32.940
Then the onions won't be grilled.

00:18:33.310 --> 00:18:36.190
But aren't the onions just a topping?

00:18:36.190 --> 00:18:37.900
You have no idea...

00:18:37.940 --> 00:18:38.730
W-Well...

00:18:38.730 --> 00:18:40.190
Wouldn't they both work...?

00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:44.780
Do you think the fat end or thin
end of a chocolate cornet is the head?

00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:47.200
The fat end?

00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:49.200
We think the same.

00:18:49.200 --> 00:18:49.620
Seriously?

00:18:50.120 --> 00:18:51.620
Then which end do you start eating from?

00:18:52.540 --> 00:18:53.830
Don't you cut off the thin end...

00:18:53.830 --> 00:18:55.880
...and eat it with the excess chocolate?

00:19:03.800 --> 00:19:07.890
Have you ever made any real-life friends besides us?

00:19:08.930 --> 00:19:12.770
I guess I had a really close friend back in middle school.

00:19:13.480 --> 00:19:14.730
So you had one.

00:19:15.310 --> 00:19:17.690
I haven't been in touch for a while...

00:19:17.690 --> 00:19:19.610
Wonder what she's up to...

00:19:22.240 --> 00:19:24.860
She wrote in our graduation book...

00:19:24.860 --> 00:19:26.700
...that her dream was to become a wizard.

00:19:26.700 --> 00:19:27.910
So she was one of your kind?!

00:19:33.610 --> 00:19:34.920
Good lucky!

00:19:35.330 --> 00:19:38.130
It's finally time for Lucky Channel!

00:19:38.130 --> 00:19:39.960
Now being broadcast on TV!

00:19:39.960 --> 00:19:40.420
Okay!

00:19:40.960 --> 00:19:42.960
Hello to everyone who's meeting us for the first time!

00:19:42.960 --> 00:19:45.470
I'll be your navigator, Akira Kogami.

00:19:46.430 --> 00:19:47.220
I'm Shiraishi.

00:19:49.220 --> 00:19:49.930
Who're you?

00:19:49.930 --> 00:19:51.220
Just kidding!

00:19:51.220 --> 00:19:54.020
This person will be helping me out now.

00:19:54.020 --> 00:19:55.560
Minoru Shiraishi-san!

00:19:55.560 --> 00:19:56.520
Da-dada-dum!

00:19:57.230 --> 00:19:58.110
Uh...

00:19:58.110 --> 00:20:00.610
I'll be serving as Akira-sama's assistant.

00:20:00.610 --> 00:20:02.280
I'm Minoru Shiraishi.

00:20:02.280 --> 00:20:02.780
Nice to meet you.

00:20:03.030 --> 00:20:04.030
Say what?

00:20:04.030 --> 00:20:05.780
You're such a stick-in-the-mud.

00:20:05.950 --> 00:20:06.860
Come on.

00:20:06.860 --> 00:20:08.490
We're on TV now.

00:20:08.490 --> 00:20:10.200
Be more crazy!

00:20:10.200 --> 00:20:10.740
Just kidding!

00:20:10.740 --> 00:20:11.540
Sorry.

00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:12.160
I'm not used to this.

00:20:12.450 --> 00:20:12.990
Okay!

00:20:12.990 --> 00:20:14.000
Let's get rollin'!

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:16.870
We've received commemorative
postcards from lots of people!

00:20:16.870 --> 00:20:17.750
Ah, right.

00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:18.630
Um...

00:20:18.630 --> 00:20:21.420
This is from Berryz Lover in Osaka.

00:20:21.920 --> 00:20:24.760
Congratulations on Lucky Channel making it to TV.

00:20:24.760 --> 00:20:25.670
Thanks!

00:20:25.800 --> 00:20:28.340
By the way, I have a question for Akira-san.

00:20:28.340 --> 00:20:31.350
You are a well-known super idol.

00:20:31.350 --> 00:20:33.600
How much exactly is an idol paid?

00:20:33.600 --> 00:20:34.680
Please let me know.

00:20:38.310 --> 00:20:39.060
Pay?

00:20:40.690 --> 00:20:43.400
That's a rather direct question.

00:20:43.600 --> 00:20:45.320
Y'know...

00:20:45.320 --> 00:20:47.400
What's the point in even asking that?

00:20:47.400 --> 00:20:48.610
A-Akira-sama?

00:20:48.610 --> 00:20:50.990
Well, if you really want to know, I'll tell you.

00:20:50.990 --> 00:20:52.530
To be frank, it jumps all over.

00:20:52.530 --> 00:20:54.290
Sometimes, it's just cheap pay...

00:20:54.290 --> 00:20:55.540
...and then there's your agency.

00:20:55.540 --> 00:20:57.120
I'm still on a fixed salary...

00:20:57.120 --> 00:20:59.880
...so who knows how much they're skimming off.

00:21:00.080 --> 00:21:02.540
And I've been working since I was three...

00:21:02.540 --> 00:21:05.300
...so all the money still goes to my parents.

00:21:05.300 --> 00:21:07.970
They, like, give me an allowance.

00:21:07.970 --> 00:21:10.090
And boy, do they skimp.

00:21:10.590 --> 00:21:13.850
Come to think of it, Mama's been
buying a bunch of name brand purses recently.

00:21:13.850 --> 00:21:16.060
Is she paying for that with the money from this show?

00:21:16.200 --> 00:21:17.850
Don't mess with me!

00:21:17.850 --> 00:21:18.770
Am I supposed to be Cinderella?!

00:21:18.770 --> 00:21:19.640
Wait...

00:21:19.640 --> 00:21:21.650
Just because Papa hasn't
sent you any money recently...

00:21:21.650 --> 00:21:22.190
Hold on!

00:21:22.190 --> 00:21:22.400
...doesn't make me your piggy bank!
Hold on!

00:21:22.400 --> 00:21:24.440
You don't have to bring that up!
...doesn't make me your piggy bank!

00:21:25.610 --> 00:21:26.610
Oh no!

00:21:26.610 --> 00:21:28.530
It's time to say goodbye!

00:21:28.530 --> 00:21:29.650
Akira's so sad!

00:21:30.100 --> 00:21:31.110
And so...

00:21:31.110 --> 00:21:37.660
Send us any questions or
comments about the show please!

00:21:37.660 --> 00:21:39.830
Shiraishi-san, ask them with a please!

00:21:40.580 --> 00:21:43.210
Then we hope you'll be back next time.

00:21:43.210 --> 00:21:44.590
See ya!

00:21:45.710 --> 00:21:46.340
Oh, yeah.

00:21:46.340 --> 00:21:48.760
Are you seriously going to show up in the actual show?

00:21:49.630 --> 00:21:50.880
Who told you that?

00:21:52.600 --> 00:21:55.180
The four of us don't karaoke together very often.

00:21:55.180 --> 00:21:58.350
I rarely come to these places.

00:21:58.390 --> 00:21:59.230
C'mon. C'mon.

00:21:59.230 --> 00:22:01.850
We only have two hours so start singing!

00:22:01.850 --> 00:22:03.440
You don't need to rush us.

00:22:03.440 --> 00:22:04.810
We still have time.

00:22:04.810 --> 00:22:07.280
This is kind of exciting.

00:22:07.280 --> 00:22:08.990
It's really fun.

00:22:08.990 --> 00:22:10.820
It feels really good when you sing.

00:22:10.820 --> 00:22:11.200
Huh?

00:22:11.200 --> 00:22:12.160
Where's the catalog?

00:22:12.160 --> 00:22:12.950
Catalog?

00:22:13.280 --> 00:22:14.120
The catalog.

00:22:14.120 --> 00:22:15.330
The catalog, is it?

00:22:15.330 --> 00:22:15.990
You know.

00:22:15.990 --> 00:22:17.580
The thing with all the song numbers in it.

00:22:18.080 --> 00:22:18.830
This?

00:22:18.830 --> 00:22:19.330
Yes.

00:22:19.330 --> 00:22:20.870
Then I'll start!

00:22:20.870 --> 00:22:21.960
You move fast!

00:22:22.500 --> 00:22:24.080
And she already ordered three songs!

00:22:24.080 --> 00:22:26.500
It'll be a waste if you don't load up the list.

00:22:29.210 --> 00:22:31.010
What's this song?

00:22:31.010 --> 00:22:33.720
Space Ironmen Kyodain!

00:22:33.720 --> 00:22:35.680
You've gotta start with this one!

00:22:35.680 --> 00:22:37.260
Never heard of it.

00:22:37.260 --> 00:22:38.890
Go for it, Kona-chan!

00:22:38.890 --> 00:22:39.850
Konata!

00:22:39.850 --> 00:22:40.930
You're too loud!

00:22:42.390 --> 00:22:44.270
Turn it down!

00:22:45.900 --> 00:22:48.400
Why does she know this song?

00:23:22.980 --> 00:23:24.560
Well, next time on Lucky Star:

00:23:25.010 --> 00:23:26.060
I'm Konata.

00:23:26.390 --> 00:23:27.530
So sleepy...

00:23:27.530 --> 00:23:29.920
Why am I always so sleepy...

00:23:29.920 --> 00:23:32.570
...the day after I get a lot of sleep?

00:23:32.570 --> 00:23:34.960
Doesn't that defeat the purpose of sleeping a lot?

00:23:34.960 --> 00:23:35.930
Next time:

00:23:35.950 --> 00:23:38.000
Effort and Results.

00:23:38.000 --> 00:23:39.120
Look forward to next time!
